WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
You need to be OK with being
bad to start because sucking

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.510
is the first step to being
sort of good at something.

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:10.100
I'm gonna teach
you everything I've

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:13.490
learned as cofounder of
Reddit and an investor

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:15.710
in multiple billion
dollar companies

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:19.010
so that you can go from your
own idea to actually executing

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:22.580
your dreams. There
is no shortage of things

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:23.660
that need to be improved.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:25.640
It's about realizing
what you're gonna work on

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:27.870
and then how to
actually get started.

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:31.159
Most good ideas have
lots of competitors.

00:00:31.159 --> 00:00:32.659
You should listen
to your customers.

00:00:32.659 --> 00:00:34.340
You should listen
to their customers

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.395
but pay no attention
to what they're doing.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:43.690
The best way to break in is
building the most basic version

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:46.900
of your product, and
even if it's janky,

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:48.730
it's proof of execution.

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:50.198
If you're meeting with
an investor, what

00:00:50.198 --> 00:00:52.240
you've got to get across
in the first few minutes

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:55.210
is that there's a clear problem,
a clear need, and a huge market

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:57.070
opportunity if we get it right.

00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:58.180
Let's get started.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:01.500
[MUSIC PLAYING]

